From c64c5dcfefed2dc04534daace78353522f4122eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qineng-det <det@topogym.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] cuda: reproducible linear solve (TopoGym determinism
 series 1/4)

Replaces the float atomics on the global linear solve path with fixed-order
sums. Physics unchanged; only the summation order is fixed, so identical
inputs give bit-identical iterates in every process (same GPU model).

Atomics replaced:
- linear_fused_pcg.cu fused_dot: per-warp sums atomicAdd'ed into d_result
  -> det::sum (det_reduce.h): every thread sums a fixed index set, a
  cub::BlockReduce per block, and the last block to finish (integer atomic
  counter) sums the per-block partials in index order; one launch.
- spmv.cu Spmv::rbk_sym_spmv / rbk_sym_spmv_dot as used by
  GlobalLinearSystem (symmetric BCOO, one triangle stored): row segments
  added across warps with atomic adds, the transposed half
  y_j += A_ij^T x_i scattered with atomic adds, warp dot sums atomicAdd'ed
  -> DetSymSpmv (det_spmv.h): after every assembly, an integer-only plan
  (cub radix sort of (row, col) keys) expands A into a row-sorted block CSR
  with both triangles (blocks copied, transposed where needed) and splits
  the block rows into short rows (< 33 blocks) and long rows (the
  affine-body rows that touch many contacts). The SpMV gives each short
  row 4 lanes (lane l sums blocks l, l + 4, ... in order; a fixed xor
  butterfly combines them) and each long row a whole thread block (a fixed
  cub::BlockReduce tree); both loop over their row lists with a fixed
  grid stride. The fused dot sums each lane group's rows in loop order,
  each thread block's groups in group order, and the last thread block
  to finish sums the per-block partials in index order.

Checks: the same assembled system solved twice in one process: solution
entries that differ, rope_threading medium 15009 of 15165 -> 0 (55
solves), knot_untying medium K2 0 of 96852 (244 solves); PCG iteration
counts equal. Kernel time on the same matrix in the same process (stock /
this patch, SpMV, SpMV + dot): rope medium (5055 block rows, longest row
206 blocks) 8.2 / 8.3 us, 11.2 / 10.3 us; knot medium (32284 block rows,
longest row 883 blocks) 22.4 / 22.5 us, 26.7 / 26.4 us.
